# QueueFlow environment - copy to `.env` in the repository root and fill in.
# `.env` is git-ignored: never commit real values. Everything below is an
# example; generate your own secrets.
#
# Two ways to run QueueFlow read this file:
# - Local development (dev.ps1 + compose.yaml): PostgreSQL in Docker, the
#   backend and the Vite dev server on this machine.
# - Production-style Docker stack (compose.prod.yaml): PostgreSQL, backend
#   and nginx-served frontend all in containers, at http://localhost:8088.
# Each variable says which of them uses it.

# ===== PostgreSQL (both) =====
# The database, user and password of the PostgreSQL container. Local
# development and the Docker stack each have their own database volume.
POSTGRES_DB=queueflow
POSTGRES_USER=queueflow
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me

# ===== Backend database connection (local development only) =====
# How the backend running on this machine reaches PostgreSQL. Match the
# values above. The Docker stack sets these itself (DB_HOST=postgres,
# DB_PORT=5432, the rest from POSTGRES_*), so they are not used there.
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=5432
DB_NAME=queueflow
DB_USERNAME=queueflow
DB_PASSWORD=change-me

# ===== Security / JWT (both, required) =====
# Base64-encoded HS256 key of at least 32 bytes. The backend refuses to start
# without it, and the Docker stack refuses to start without it. Generate your
# own, e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`, and never commit it. Tokens last
# 1 hour (queueflow.security.jwt.ttl in application.yml).
JWT_SECRET=<base64-encoded-random-32-bytes>

# ===== CORS (optional) =====
# Exact browser origins allowed to call the backend from another origin,
# comma-separated; wildcards are rejected. Defaults to the Vite dev server,
# http://localhost:5173. Not needed by the Docker stack: there the browser
# reaches the API through nginx on the page's own origin.
# QUEUEFLOW_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173

# ===== Frontend (local development only) =====
# The backend's origin for the Vite dev server (no trailing /api), read from
# this file (vite.config.ts envDir); only VITE_* variables reach the browser.
# The Docker stack ignores it and builds its frontend with "/" (same origin).
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# ===== Docker stack (optional) =====
# The port the stack is published on, on this machine only (127.0.0.1).
# APP_PORT=8088
